From b4db3be86e03ec31055303d46056223bb989472e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amaury Denoyelle <adenoyelle@haproxy.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Jan 2024 14:39:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] BUG/MINOR: server: fix server_find_by_name() usage during
 parsing

Since below commit, server_find_by_name() now search using
'used_server_id' proxy backend tree :
  4bcfe30414005323a8d4ab986bce92bb736b59df
  OPTIM: server: eb lookup for server_find_by_name()

This introduces a regression if server_find_by_name() is used via
check_config_validity() during post-parsing. Indeed, used_server_id tree
is populated at the same stage so it's possible to not found an existing
server. This can cause incorrect rejection of previously valid
configuration file.

To fix this, servers are now inserted in used_server_id tree during
parsing via parse_server(). This guarantees that server instances can be
retrieved during post parsing.

A known feature which uses server_find_by_name() during post parsing is
attach-srv tcp-rule used for reverse HTTP. Prior to the current fix, a
config was wrongly rejected if the rule was declared before the server
line.

This should not be backported unless the mentionned commit is.

diff --git a/src/cfgparse.c b/src/cfgparse.c
index fc1ab8a30..feab258e0 100644
--- a/src/cfgparse.c
+++ b/src/cfgparse.c
@@ -3658,8 +3658,6 @@ int check_config_validity()
 				newsrv->conf.id.key = newsrv->puid = next_id;
 				eb32_insert(&curproxy->conf.used_server_id, &newsrv->conf.id);
 			}
-			newsrv->conf.name.key = newsrv->id;
-			ebis_insert(&curproxy->conf.used_server_name, &newsrv->conf.name);

 			next_id++;
 			newsrv = newsrv->next;

diff --git a/src/server.c b/src/server.c
index 147b1947d..b35d16caa 100644
--- a/src/server.c
+++ b/src/server.c
@@ -3008,6 +3008,9 @@ static int _srv_parse_tmpl_init(struct server *srv, struct proxy *px)
 		/* Linked backwards first. This will be restablished after parsing. */
 		newsrv->next = px->srv;
 		px->srv = newsrv;
+
+		newsrv->conf.name.key = newsrv->id;
+		ebis_insert(&curproxy->conf.used_server_name, &newsrv->conf.name);
 	}
 	_srv_parse_set_id_from_prefix(srv, srv->tmpl_info.prefix, srv->tmpl_info.nb_low);

@@ -3525,8 +3528,13 @@ int parse_server(const char *file, int linenum, char **args,
 			goto out;
 	}

-	if (parse_flags & SRV_PARSE_TEMPLATE)
+	if (parse_flags & SRV_PARSE_TEMPLATE) {
 		_srv_parse_tmpl_init(newsrv, curproxy);
+	}
+	else if (!(parse_flags & SRV_PARSE_DEFAULT_SERVER)) {
+		newsrv->conf.name.key = newsrv->id;
+		ebis_insert(&curproxy->conf.used_server_name, &newsrv->conf.name);
+	}

 	/* If the server id is fixed, insert it in the proxy used_id tree.
 	 * This is needed to detect a later duplicate id via srv_parse_id.
-- 
2.25.1

### Modifications in Each File

1. **File: `src/cfgparse.c`**
   - Removed the insertion of the server's name into the `used_server_name` tree during the `check_config_validity()` function. This was previously done with the lines:
     ```c
     newsrv->conf.name.key = newsrv->id;
     ebis_insert(&curproxy->conf.used_server_name, &newsrv->conf.name);
     ```
   - The insertion of the server's ID into the `used_server_id` tree remains unchanged.

2. **File: `src/server.c`**
   - Added the insertion of the server's name into the `used_server_name` tree during the server parsing process. This is done in two places:
     - In the `_srv_parse_tmpl_init()` function, right after linking the new server instance:
       ```c
       newsrv->conf.name.key = newsrv->id;
       ebis_insert(&curproxy->conf.used_server_name, &newsrv->conf.name);
       ```
     - In the `parse_server()` function, under a condition that checks if the server is not a template or a default server:
       ```c
       else if (!(parse_flags & SRV_PARSE_DEFAULT_SERVER)) {
           newsrv->conf.name.key = newsrv->id;
           ebis_insert(&curproxy->conf.used_server_name, &newsrv->conf.name);
       }
       ```

### Relationships Between Modifications

The modifications in `src/cfgparse.c` and `src/server.c` are interrelated in addressing a regression introduced by a previous commit that changed how server instances are looked up. The removal of the server name insertion in `check_config_validity()` could lead to incorrect configuration rejections during post-parsing, as the `used_server_name` tree would not contain the necessary entries. 

To resolve this, the patch ensures that server names are inserted into the `used_server_name` tree during the parsing phase in `src/server.c`. This guarantees that when `server_find_by_name()` is called during post-parsing (as in the case of the `attach-srv` tcp-rule), the server instances can be correctly retrieved, thus preventing the erroneous rejection of valid configurations. 

Overall, the changes ensure that server instances are properly registered in both the `used_server_id` and `used_server_name` trees at the appropriate times, maintaining the integrity of the configuration validation process.

